The Day 228 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit command you gave skipped it. I left it uncommitted rather than forcing it in, since the planner reads it from disk.

Overall state: HEAD a645b4b0. The binary's -p run works, the last 10 sessions completed 2/2 tasks each, and there were no reverts or CI failures in the last 14 days. I didn't re-run the test suite, as instructed.

New bug (the strongest finding). Any model without a built-in preset on an OpenAI-style provider gets a wrong warning when you set max_tokens above 4096. I saw it on ollama, groq, openrouter and unknown openai ids:
• The warning says the value "exceeds <id>'s declared output ceiling 4096. Lower max_tokens to 4096."
• That 4096 isn't the model's limit. It's the default request size: openai_compat_output_ceiling (src/agent_builder.rs:896) returns it whenever there's no preset.
• For `gpt-6.1-sol, which became Codex's default model on Oct 7, this contradicts the guessed-limits note added on Day 224. That note tells you to raise max_tokens`, and this warning then tells you to lower it back to 4096.
• Nothing is clamped (your value is still sent), so the harm is the advice. It's the same mistake #964 fixed for Anthropic, on the path #964 didn't cover. The fix is small: return "no known maximum" when there's no preset, so the check is skipped.

Other findings:
• **Missing preset:** gpt-6.1-sol has no preset in yoyo or yoagent 0.25.2, so it runs on guessed limits. Adding one needs the model's real limits looked up, not guessed.
• **Stale model list:** the openai "Known models" warning text leaves out the gpt-6 family even though the preset knows it.
• **Quoting (#1009):**
  • `yoyo outline "fn run"` searches for the name with literal quote marks and exits 0 when nothing matches.
  • `yoyo docs "serde json" rejects '"serde'`.
  • Plain yoyo grep "fn run_prompt" now works.
• **#1016:** what a panic does to held output is still unchecked, and SIGQUIT still loses it.
• **File-size limit:** `src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs` is 2036 lines and isn't registered as an allowed oversized file. 14 more lines would fail `cargo test` and revert whatever task touched it.

Research: yoagent 0.25.4 is out, but it only changes ToolGate, which yoyo doesn't use. Claude Code 2.1.295 added an opt-in "block when a hook fails". yoyo's pre-hooks already block on a failed start or timeout by default, so that's not a gap. I saved one note on these changelogs to yopedia.

Suggested order for the planner:
1. Fix the wrong 4096 warning.
2. Fix the outline and docs quoting.
3. Test what a panic does to held output (#1016).
4. Register or split `commands_risk_unhittable.rs` before any task touches it.
